Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage to answer:  
• Dim_CensusMetrics."MetricTableID": find the ACS table that deals with commute times (B08303 – “Travel Time to Work”).  
• Dim_CensusMetrics."MetricID": the unique key that represents each commute–time bucket (e.g., “B08303_013E” = “60 minutes or more”).  
• Dim_CensusMetrics."Descriptor1"/"Descriptor2"/"Descriptor3": text phrases ( “…60 minutes or more…”) that help isolate the right MetricID for “> 1 hour”.  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip."MetricID": join to census values that are already rolled‑up to the Zip‑Code level.  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip."CensusValueByZip": the commuter counts by Zip.  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip."ZipCode": join key to geography.  
• LU_GeographyExpanded."ZipCode": join key.  
• LU_GeographyExpanded."PreferredStateAbbrev": limits the search to “NY”.  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."MetricID": join to bring in the New‑York statewide benchmark for the exact commute‑time bucket.  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."StateAbbrev": restrict to “NY”.  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."StateBenchmarkValue": statewide commuters over one hour.  
• Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021."TotalStatePopulation": 2021 total state population.  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• Dim_CensusMetrics."MetricTableID" = 'B08303'  
• ( "Descriptor1" ILIKE '%60%' OR "Descriptor2" ILIKE '%60%' OR "Descriptor3" ILIKE '%60%' )  
• LU_GeographyExpanded."PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each) that progressively build toward the answer.

```sql
--Description: 1) Peek at the metrics table to understand overall structure.
SELECT *
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Dim_CensusMetrics"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) See every ACS table represented, looking for commute tables.
SELECT DISTINCT "MetricTableID"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Dim_CensusMetrics"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Pull all metrics from table B08303 (Travel Time to Work).
SELECT "MetricID",
       "MetricTableID",
       "MetricTableDesc",
       "Descriptor1",
       "Descriptor2",
       "Descriptor3"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Dim_CensusMetrics"
WHERE "MetricTableID" = 'B08303'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Narrow to rows whose descriptors mention “60” or “minutes” (good proxy for “> 1 hour”).
SELECT "MetricID",
       "MetricTableDesc",
       "Descriptor1",
       "Descriptor2",
       "Descriptor3"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Dim_CensusMetrics"
WHERE "MetricTableID" = 'B08303'
  AND ( "Descriptor1" ILIKE '%60%' 
        OR "Descriptor2" ILIKE '%60%' 
        OR "Descriptor3" ILIKE '%60%' )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) View some Zip‑level commuter values for all B08303 metrics.
SELECT f."ZipCode",
       f."MetricID",
       f."CensusValueByZip"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip" f
WHERE f."MetricID" LIKE 'B08303%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Join the previous list to the metric descriptors so we can read what each value means.
SELECT f."ZipCode",
       f."CensusValueByZip",
       m."MetricID",
       m."Descriptor1",
       m."Descriptor2",
       m."Descriptor3"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip" f
JOIN "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Dim_CensusMetrics" m
      ON f."MetricID" = m."MetricID"
WHERE m."MetricTableID" = 'B08303'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Add geography; restrict to New York Zip codes; still show every B08303 bucket.
SELECT g."ZipCode",
       m."MetricID",
       m."Descriptor1",
       f."CensusValueByZip"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip" f
JOIN "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."LU_GeographyExpanded" g
      ON f."ZipCode" = g."ZipCode"
JOIN "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Dim_CensusMetrics" m
      ON f."MetricID" = m."MetricID"
WHERE g."PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'
  AND m."MetricTableID" = 'B08303'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Only keep the “60 minutes or more” MetricID and rank NY Zip codes by commuters.
SELECT g."ZipCode",
       f."CensusValueByZip" AS "Commuters_60Plus"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021_ByZip" f
JOIN "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."LU_GeographyExpanded" g
      ON f."ZipCode" = g."ZipCode"
WHERE g."PreferredStateAbbrev" = 'NY'
  AND f."MetricID"  = 'B08303_013E'     -- assume 60+ minutes bucket after confirming in step 4
ORDER BY "Commuters_60Plus" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Retrieve New York’s statewide benchmark for the exact same MetricID.
SELECT s."MetricID",
       s."StateBenchmarkValue",
       s."TotalStatePopulation"
FROM "CENSUS_GALAXY__AIML_MODEL_DATA_ENRICHMENT_SAMPLE"."PUBLIC"."Fact_StateBenchmark_ACS2021" s
WHERE s."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
